Back with my Arduino LEDs! This time, I programmed them to turn on when a button is pressed and turn off when released. Each new press turns on a different random LED.

**Code it**

For this assignment, I used while loops, random(), and state variables. The while loops helped me keep the LED on while the button was pressed and avoid selecting the same LED twice in a row.

I also used previousPin to remember the last LED that was turned on.

##Tips

Pay attention in class. Most of what you need is already covered.

Be careful with while loops. Make sure your loop can eventually stop.

Test as you go. It makes finding and fixing mistakes much easier.

